-- title:
--   Every polynomial has a Chebyshev expansion
-- statement:
--   Let $Q$ be a real polynomial of degree at most $d$, and let $T_j$ denote the Chebyshev polynomials of the first kind. There are real coefficients $c_0,\dots,c_d$ with
--   $$
--   Q=\sum_{j=0}^dc_j\,T_j .
--   $$
--
--   The Chebyshev polynomials $T_0,\dots,T_d$ form a basis of the polynomials of degree at most $d$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/ChebyshevBounds.lean#L114-L130

